# PostHog — register new pages

When adding a **new user-facing route or static page**, also update PostHog page context so analytics do not fall through to `page_key: other`.

## Required

1. Add `PAGE_META` entry (`page_key` → `page_name`, `page_group`)
2. Add a `ROUTE_RULES` match (more specific rules first); update `STATIC_PAGE_KEYS` for static HTML paths
3. Keep **both** files in sync:
   - `src/lib/posthog-page-context.js`
   - `public/js/posthog-page-context.js`

## Skip only when

- Pure API / cron / internal dashboard-only endpoints with no user pageview
- Redirect-only stubs that never render a page

Full rule: `docs/ops/POSTHOG-PAGE-CONTEXT.md`
